1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,227
Can OpusClip clip a live stream?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:03,933
No.

3
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:09,233
OpusClip's own help center says uploading while you're still streaming isn't supported.

4
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:11,914
You wait for the stream to end, then upload.

5
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:15,569
ClipMe's engine clips live Kick, Twitch and YouTube streams.

6
00:00:16,519 --> 00:00:21,743
OpusClip is built around a finished file, and its free plan doesn't take Twitch links.

7
00:00:21,743 --> 00:00:24,476
ClipMe's engine reads the live stream itself.

8
00:00:25,426 --> 00:00:31,506
It ranks moments with a multi-signal model, and on Kick and Twitch, chat activity is one of the signals.

9
00:00:32,456 --> 00:00:34,851
There's no per-minute credit meter.

10
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:39,709
ClipMe's Starter plan is free with a watermark, and Pro is $29 a month.

11
00:00:40,659 --> 00:00:43,934
See every OpusClip alternative at clipme.com.

12
00:00:43,934 --> 00:00:45,971
Paste a VOD and try it free.

